# User entry + skill discipline

## For the user

| Slash | For |
|-------|-----|
| `/ask-install` | Install this kit into the product workspace (see `INSTALL.md`) |
| `/ask-requirement` | Product/code work now |
| `/ask-backlog` | Park an idea without cutting focus |

If the project has its own local environment (Docker/PM2/etc.), add its slash commands here following the same pattern with the `ask-` prefix (e.g. `/ask-bootstrap`, `/ask-start-local`, `/ask-stop-local`) and document them in a project-owned `ask-local-env-shared` skill.

- Do not ask the user to choose among internal skills (`/speckit-*`, `/ask-orchestrate-*`, framework details, etc.).
- Those skills are **agent-only** (`disable-model-invocation: true`); the orchestrator invokes them.

## Shared pack (agents)

| Skill | For |
|-------|-----|
| `ask-agent-skill-discipline` | Do not improvise; gaps; self-improve |
| `ask-git-project` | Commits, branches, PRs, multi-repo |
| `ask-agent-knowledge` | Pointer to `agent-knowledge/AGENTS.md` |

If a shared skill is missing → `SKILL GAP` → create/extend the skill + update the project's role docs (if any).

## Discipline

- Every procedure → an existing skill (shared or role).
- Don't know → declare a gap and improve the skill.
- Detail: `.cursor/skills/ask-agent-skill-discipline/SKILL.md`
